# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ccadapt/.gitignore
#
# Policy: the repo commits CODE + CONFIG + TEXT only. Every byte in the data
# folders is reproducible by re-running the pipeline (or clearly documented
# as a manual drop in data/inputs/MANIFEST.md), so none of it belongs in
# version control.
#
# If you need to share a reproduced output with collaborators, push it to the
# team S3 bucket under the `cca` STAC collection rather than committing it.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Downloaded / generated data ----------------------------------------
# Everything the pipeline fetches (GADM, Naturebase, Sanderman, ERA, FAO,
# MapSPAM, WorldClim, SoilGrids, etc.) is either auto-fetchable via
# code/inputs/*.R or a documented manual drop. The Naturebase bundle
# (data/naturebase/**, ~500 MB unzipped) is fetched by fetch_naturebase.R.
# Reference PDFs under data/papers/ are personal copies and kept off the
# public repo; a bibliography file stays if you add one later.
data/inputs/**
data/staging/**
data/outputs/**
data/naturebase/**
data/papers/**

# Keep the MANIFEST + folder stubs so new clones know where to drop data.
!data/inputs/
!data/inputs/MANIFEST.md
!data/staging/
!data/staging/.gitkeep
!data/outputs/
!data/outputs/.gitkeep

# ---- Policy / scoping PDFs (may be embargoed) --------------------------
text/policy/**

# ---- Investment / proposal documents (contain internal grant IDs) -------
# The pipeline reads scope from practices.yaml and neb_config.yaml, not from
# the investment document, so keeping it off version control is safe.
text/Investment Document*.docx
text/Investment Document*.pdf
text/INV-*

# ---- Logs + scratch -----------------------------------------------------
*.log
fetch.log
*.out

# ---- R artefacts --------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj.user/
*-Ex.R
/*.tar.gz
/*.Rcheck/

# ---- Python / Jupyter artefacts (if ever added) ------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- OS cruft -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- Editor / IDE -------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.project
.Rproj.user
*.Rproj

# ---- Temporary / partial download files --------------------------------
*.part
*.tmp
*.bak

# ---- Large raster / vector products (defensive, redundant with data/**)
*.tif
*.tiff
*.gpkg
*.geojson
*.parquet
*.gz
*.zip
*.nc
*.nc4

# ---- BUT keep small example / config rasters if any are ever committed
!examples/**/*.tif
